# Activity 6: Making a Personal Portfolio Website

## Description
This activity involved designing and documenting a responsive one-page **Personal Portfolio Website** for **Nicole Pauleen "Leen" Fuentes**[cite: 71, 72]. Built with a soft blush-pink, cream, and rose aesthetic, the site presents my Home introduction, About Me story, BS Nursing education at Ateneo de Davao University, core strengths, personal hobbies, goals, and contact information[cite: 71, 72, 73, 74, 75].

## What Have I Learned?
- **Key Concepts & Skills:** I learned how to translate personal and academic information into a structured web layout using clear navigation links, rounded content cards, and cohesive color psychology to create a welcoming first impression[cite: 71, 72, 76].
- **Challenge & Solution:** Deciding how to balance academic nursing aspirations with personal hobbies without cluttering a single-page layout was a challenge; I solved this by separating content into distinct, scannable sections with concise card descriptions[cite: 71, 72, 74, 76].
- **Future Application & Improvement:** I can expand this portfolio as I complete more clinical rotations and nursing research projects, and I could improve it by adding interactive links to my downloadable resume and completed academic works.
